  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511512578047-dfb367046420?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Unlock Ascend early and use it as a primary traversal tool; most combat encounters can be entirely bypassed by ascending through ceilings to high ground.",
      "Fuse weapons to a minimum of 30+ attack rating before entering any Colosseum or dungeon—unfused weapons break within one or two encounters against Gloom-stat enemies.",
      "Collect Flint and Amber in bulk from Zora's Domain cave systems; these two materials power the cheapest Battery upgrade path and speed up the Construct Factory quests.",
      "In Depths exploration, deploy Brightbloom Seeds every 30 steps rather than on demand—running into Gloom damage without light restores is the single biggest HP drain in early Depths runs.",
      "Convert Zonai Devices into Zonai Charges rather than carrying them unless you have an active construction goal; inventory weight management significantly affects puzzle throughput."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "「トオルカ」を早期に解放し、主要移動手段として使う。天井を突き抜ける機動力で多くの戦闘を回避できる。",
      "コロシアムやダンジョン突入前に武器の攻撃力を合計30以上に強化する。強化なしだとグルームステータス敵に1〜2回の戦闘で折れる。",
      "ゾーラ地方の洞窟でクリントとコハクを大量に集める。バッテリーアップグレードの最安ルートで、建造台クエストも加速できる。",
      "地底探索中は30歩ごとにヒカリゴケの種を使う。照明なしでグルームダメージを受けると、序盤の地底周回で最大のHP損失源になる。",
      "建造目的がない場合はゾナウギアをゾナウエネルギーに変換して持ち歩く。インベントリ管理がパズル解法の速度に直結する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Sky Island Priority: Ability Unlock Order",
        "body": "Clear the four tutorial shrines in this order for maximum early mobility: Ukouh Shrine (Ultrahand) → In-isa Shrine (Fuse) → Gutanbac Shrine (Ascend) → Nachoyah Shrine (Recall). Completing them in this sequence gives you Ascend before reaching the final Sky Island platform, which opens a shortcut that skips the Construct puzzle section and saves approximately 8 minutes of first-playthrough time."
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Rupee and Material Loop",
        "body": "Farm Bubbulfrog caves in the Necluda region first—each cave yields 1 Bubbulgemand a guaranteed chest. Sell Bubbulgems to Koltin for bonus inventory slots rather than rupees in early game. For combat materials, the Akkala Depths entrance has the highest Zonaite node density, providing early Battery upgrade resources without fighting difficult enemies."
      },
      {
        "title": "First Shrine Routing",
        "body": "Target Light Root shrines in the Depths directly below Surface shrines to double-dip on fast travel nodes. The Hyrule Castle Depths Light Root unlocks both a Surface and Underground fast travel point simultaneously. Getting 20 shrines before the first temple dramatically smooths the stamina wheel upgrade path and keeps combat options open against field minibosses."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Fuse Loadout Standardisation",
        "body": "Maintain two standard fuse presets: a utility set (Rock Octopus eye for night vision, Chuchu Jelly for element vs. Construct type) and a damage set (Silver Lizalfos horn or Lizalfos tail for high flat damage). Rebuilding fuse loadouts from scratch mid-dungeon costs 40–60 seconds per encounter and disrupts rhythm significantly during timed challenge rooms."
      },
      {
        "title": "Dungeon Boss Preparation",
        "body": "Each temple boss is defeated faster with an element-specific weapon: Fire Temple requires ice-fused weapons, Water Temple prefers electric fused. Farm the relevant Chuchu Jelly colour from Eventide Island or Lanayru Wetlands the session before tackling each temple. Stockpile 10+ of the matching element before entry rather than farming mid-dungeon."
      },
      {
        "title": "Depths Dark Root Mapping",
        "body": "The Depths have 120 Light Roots mirroring each Surface shrine. Unlock Light Roots in clusters by fast-travelling to a known root and walking toward the bright glow on the minimap. Cover the Eldin Underground and Faron Underground quadrants before the Akkala and Necluda quadrants—the former two have higher Zonaite yield and lower Gloom enemy density per Light Root."
      },
      {
        "title": "Autobuild and Construction Shortcuts",
        "body": "The Autobuild ability stores up to five previous constructions. Build your most-used vehicle (3-fan hoverbike or 2-wheel cart) once, then use Autobuild for subsequent rebuilds. Zonaite cost for Autobuild is 3–5 charges per small vehicle; carrying 30+ spare Zonaite Charges eliminates mid-exploration construction bottlenecks entirely."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Gloom Hearts Recovery Strategy",
        "body": "Gloom Hearts from the final dungeon and Demon King encounters cannot be recovered by food. Keep 2–3 Sundelions in a dedicated hotbar slot and cook them into Sunny dishes before the Hyrule Castle assault. Each Sunny dish restores a baseline of 3 Gloom Hearts. Running out of Sunny food inside the castle is effectively a soft timer on your remaining combat capacity."
      },
      {
        "title": "Ganondorf Phase Breakdown",
        "body": "The Demon Dragon phase requires Tulin's gust to reach Ganondorf's weak points efficiently. Keep the Tulin companion active throughout the approach flight. In the final phase, the weak point recharge timer is 8 seconds; using Recall on a launched rock extends the attack window by an additional 4–5 seconds. Target the crown jewel last—it triggers the final cutscene upon destruction."
      },
      {
        "title": "Completionist Checklist Priority",
        "body": "If targeting 100% completion, finish Bubbulfrogs (147 total) before final boss to receive the reward item from Kilton. All Korok Seed deliveries to Hestu can be batched at the Korok Forest or at any camp after unlocking him—no need to travel to him for each individual seed. Memory locations are revealed via the purah pad photo album and can all be done in a single flight path using the 3-fan hoverbike."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Skipping stamina upgrades in favour of heart containers early on—Ascend and climbing traversal in the Sky Islands require sustained stamina, and insufficient wheels cause falls from critical heights.",
      "Entering the Depths without at least 20 Brightbloom Seeds and 5 Puffshroom Bombs—Gloom recovery is purely light-dependent, not item-dependent, and running dry ends exploration runs prematurely.",
      "Fusing a rare unique monster part (Silver Lynel horn) to a weapon without confirming its drop rate first—Silver Lynels have 12-minute respawn cycles, and losing a fused rare part sets back weapon optimisation significantly.",
      "Trying to solve Zonai Device puzzles with insufficient Battery charge—each Device failure drains 1.5–2 Battery cells if abandoned mid-operation; fully charge using Zonai Charges before initiating complex multi-device constructions.",
      "Fighting Phantom Ganon in the Castle courtyard before having Gloom Heart recovery food—unlike field encounters, this fight does not have a safe reset option and Gloom damage compounds over the 4-phase encounter."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "序盤にスタミナよりハートを優先する。スカイアイランドの「トオルカ」や崖登り移動には持続スタミナが必要で、不足すると致命的な落下を招く。",
      "ヒカリゴケの種20個とフワフワのキノコ5個なしで地底に入る。グルーム回復は照明依存であり、資源切れで探索が強制終了する。",
      "シルバーライネルの角など希少素材を武器に合体させる前に入手確率を確認しない。ライネルの再生成は12分サイクルで、希少合体素材の損失は装備最適化を大幅に遅らせる。",
      "バッテリー残量不足でゾナウギアのパズルを開始する。途中放棄で1.5〜2セル分を消費するため、複雑な多ギア建造前は必ずゾナウエネルギーで補充する。",
